3b68b6c0-778d-440a-97f4-2f851e53be42	cicc-official-careers	151261933	中金公司	ETF Capital Markets Specialist(J19802)	https://cicc.zhiye.com/social/jobs	unknown	bachelor	experienced	unknown	collector/0.2.0	bfc0addba20b44c4f72a7b95ccb7a7684a6b63a415711d5c3e602e8243766b50	Key Responsibilities\n- Coordinate and monitor daily ETF primary market activity, including creation and redemption workflows, work with Portfolio Management, Trading, Operations, and relevant service providers such as custodian, transfer agent, and administrator\n- Monitor secondary-market quality across bid–ask spreads, premiums and discounts to net asset value (NAV), trading volumes, market depth, primary flows, and short interest; engage counterparties when pricing or liquidity deteriorates\n- Develop and manage relationships with participating dealers, market makers, liquidity providers, listing venues, and broker-dealer ETF desks\n- Partner with appointed market makers to maintain competitive spreads and market depth, resolve trading anomalies, and support seed capital placement and recall, ETF unit lending, and launch and wind-down mechanics\n- Provide capital markets inputs to Product, Portfolio Management, Legal, Compliance, Operations, and listing venues in connection with ETF launches, conversions, and liquidations\n- Serve as a subject-matter expert for Sales, client advisors, and institutional counter-parties on ETF trading mechanics, liquidity, implementation, and support best execution\n\nSkills & Competencies\n- Relationship management: builds durable, commercial relationships with participating dealers, market makers, exchanges, and internal stakeholders\n- Market-structure fluency: explains creation and redemption, arbitrage, basket design, spreads, and premium or discount behavior in precise, practical language\n- Analytical discipline: uses data to diagnose liquidity and pricing issues, review and provide input on creation/redemption baskets, and produce clear market-quality and management reporting\n- Communication: writes and presents concisely and translates technical capital markets content for portfolio managers, sales teams, and clients\n- Commercial judgement: understands how product design, listing venue, market-maker incentives, and competitor activity affect flows and the competitiveness of the ETF platform\n- Operating rigor, integrity, and collaboration: works reliably in a time-sensitive, regulated environment and partners effectively across Product, Investments, Trading, Operations, Legal, Compliance, and Sales\n- Languages: professional English and/or Chinese is required\n\nQualifications\n- Upright, humble, diligent with high moral values\n- Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Engineering, Mathematics, or a quantitative discipline; an advanced degree and/or CFA designation is preferred\n- 3-7 years’ experience in ETFs, including capital markets, ETF trading or market making, a participating dealer desk, ETF portfolio management, or a related function within asset management or a broker-dealer\n- Working knowledge of ETF legal and operational structures, creation and redemption mechanics, primary and secondary market dynamics, and pricing and liquidity drivers across one or more asset classes\n- Knowledge of ETF portfolio management is a plus, including index replication and sampling, cash management, rebalancing, tracking difference and tracking error, and the interaction between portfolio construction and the creation/redemption basket\n- Familiarity with multi-listed or cross-border ETF platforms, including US, UCITS, and Asia listings, is an advantage\n- Proficiency with Bloomberg and other market-data or surveillance tools; strong Excel and PowerPoint skills; experience with portfolio-management or order-management systems and Python or SQL is advantageous	本科	3年	2026-10-11T16:00:00.000Z	\N	\N	[]	["ai_agents", "english", "python", "sql"]	[{"skill_id": "ai_agents", "evidence_text": "custodian, transfer agent, and administrator"}, {"sk